SCRIPT='A passive-investing essay framed by Danny (active trader) vs Priya (forgot her account): SPIVA underperformance and persistence, Magellan investor-return anecdote, Dalbar behavior gap, missing best days, employer match, target-date funds, lump sum vs DCA, compounding ($500/month), Bogle fee math, account limits, Fidelity 401(k) millionaires, an honest caveat on surplus income and lower forecasts, sequence risk, simple-vs-easy discipline, a community plug and disclaimer. Verified: SPIVA 2024 summary (no category majority outperforming over 15 years), 2026 limits; Bogle, Dalbar, JPM best-days and fee arithmetic reproduce. Unverified/overstated: exact ~90% and "zero" persistence; Magellan investors "lost money"; $987K implies ~9.4%; waiting 10 years costs ~two-thirds, not half; thumbnail $50->$2M unsupported. The stored ending is complete.'
